// Steam goes along a pipe. The engine stands 3.5 m from the boiler at the head of the shaft down to the belt,
// joined to the boiler's top by copper steam pipe along the roof. Coal burns, the steam goes along the pipe, and
// the engine drives the belt. Cut the pipe and the engine has no steam: the belt stops, while the boiler goes on
// raising steam with nowhere to send it.
map
########################################
########################################
########################################
########################################
########################################
########################################
########################################
########################################
#........PPPPPPPPPPPPPPPE..............#
######..................j..............#
#wwwww..................j..............#
#wwwww..................j..............#
#wwwww..................j..............#
#wwwww..............@...*>>>>>>>>>>>...#
########################################
########################################
end
give Boiler 1
give Pickaxe 1
place 2 -11 -2 Boiler
drop 10 Coal -13 -6
drop 40 Stone 7 -1
expect 300 turning:5,0 == 1           // driven along the pipe
expect 300 zone:Stone,15,18,-1,0 == 1
pour 400 -4 -5 Granite                // the pipe cut (a fall of rock through it)
expect 500 turning:5,0 == 0
expect 500 bsteam > 15                // the boiler still raises steam, now with nowhere to send it
